From e5a4e0cc8df0c36ec82ba3b912d77662c196a43d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:31:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] infinity6c: encoder I-frame cap, I/P QP bounds and
 delta, super frames

Keyframes ran 330-370 KB at 3 Mbit/s with a 1 s GOP, nearly the whole
second's budget, and raptorctl's set-max-pic-size, set-qp-bounds,
set-qp-bounds-per-frame, set-super-frame and enc-set qp|qp_ip_delta all
answered "not supported": the backend published only bitrate, GOP, fps and
RC mode. libmi_venc.so has what they need.

- i6c_venc_rc.h (new, local: sigmastar-headers stays verbatim): the 56-byte
  MI_VENC_RcParam_t with its CBR, VBR and AVBR arms, the 16-byte super-frame
  config and the RC priority, with layout asserts, checked against the
  shipped 1230 mi.ko and libmi_venc.so (SetRcPriority takes a pointer on
  MI 3.0). Plus the pure logic: a per-channel record and the RcParam
  builder, host-tested by tests/t_venc_rc_i6c.c.
- Seven ops: enc_set_qp_bounds, enc_set_qp_bounds_per_frame,
  enc_set_qp_ip_delta, enc_set_qp, enc_set_max_pic_size and
  enc_set/get_super_frame. CBR's frame bounds go through RcParam (its
  channel attribute has none), VBR/AVBR's through the attribute with the
  I-frame bounds nested inside; fixed QP splits its I/P pair.
- The record outlives rvd's destroy/re-create for set-resolution and
  set-codec; only teardown clears it. GetRcParam never returns MaxISize or
  MaxPSize in CBR or VBR, so the HAL owns and always writes both. Every
  other field nobody asked about goes back exactly as the driver reported
  it: the driver reports MaxIPProp outside the doc's range, and raising it
  halved a VBR channel's I-frames. A released bound is MI's full range.
- RcParam is pushed after create, after every rate reapply and from each
  op. A channel nobody configured never sees SetRcParam: the default path
  makes no new MI call. A refused op is rolled back.
- Asked-for QP values clamp to MI's [12, 48] and the delta to [-12, 12],
  warned once per channel; an inverted pair from an op is RSS_ERR_INVAL,
  one from the config is swapped rather than pinning QP to the ceiling.
- Re-encode forces frame-bits-first priority: rvd always sends
  bitrate-first, under which re-encode never fires. MI's NOT_SUPPORT comes
  back as RSS_ERR_NOTSUP.
- The six MI calls bind optionally; a library without them still encodes.
- caps: has_max_pic_size, has_super_frame, has_qp_bounds_per_frame.

On an SSC377D, VBR at night: the I-frame QP bounds and the I/P delta work
(I = P - delta; -6 cut keyframes from 228 to 57 KB) and survive a mode
change and a re-create. MaxISize counts bytes and is soft: a 98 KB cap
settled 232 KB keyframes at ~130 KB, a 293 KB one did nothing
(I6C_RC_SIZE_UNIT_BITS = 8; RSS_VENC_SIZE_UNIT_BITS overrides it).
Super-frame re-encode is NOT_SUPPORT; discard is accepted.
